f the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>, completed in 1521</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1532</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a> begins the conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca Empire</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1580</span><span class="rf-text">Philip II unites the crowns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and Portugal</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1588</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Spanish Armada</a> sent against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> is defeated and wrecked by storms</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1648</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> confirms <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1898</span><span class="rf-text">Defeat by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> strips <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a></span></li></ol>
